195c6913.py-40-    Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-41-    - Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-42-    - Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-43-    - A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-44-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-45-    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-46-    - Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-47-    - On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-48-    - Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-49-    - If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-50-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-51-    Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-52-    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-53-    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-54-    H, W = g.shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-55-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-56-    template_bg = int(g[0, 0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-57-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-58-    # Path is the most frequent color != template_bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-59-    counts = Counter(map(int, g.flatten()))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-60-    path_color = int(max([(cnt, int(col